{
  "dom_id": "question-149495",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "In a nature park, there are $4$ species of squirrels, species $1$, species $2$, species $3,$ and species $4.$ Each species has the same population.\n\n- $8%$ of squirrels of species $1$ are born in captivity.\n\n- $9%$ of squirrels of species $2$ are born in captivity.\n\n- $11%$ of squirrels of species $4$ are born in captivity.\n\nIf $42%$ of the squirrels are adult females, $8%$ of the adult female squirrels are born in captivity, and $36%$ of the squirrels born in captivity are adult females, what is the probability that a randomly chosen squirrel from species $3$ is born in captivity? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "",
